{"id":"a6a4bad5449a43b5","group":"58","path":"58/batch01/58-df-zfc-model-top-extension.md","title":"ZFC Model Top Extension","display":"df-zfc-model-top-extension — ZFC Model Top Extension","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-zfc-model-top-extension","aliases":["58-df-zfc-model-top-extension"],"display":"df-zfc-model-top-extension — ZFC Model Top Extension","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-model.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-zfc-model-top-extension"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-zfc-model-top-extension</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-zfc-model-top-extension — ZFC Model Top Extension"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" href=\"?note=a3348ed9eb6fb4e3\" title=\"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md\">../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"923884eb8fe4e61d\" href=\"?note=923884eb8fe4e61d\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-model.md\">../batch09/58-df-model.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,N\\in V\">\\(M,N\\in V\\)</span> (canonical structure codes for models of set theory)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_{\\in}\">\\(L_{\\in}\\)</span> (the language with one binary relation symbol <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dot\\in\">\\(\\dot\\in\\)</span>) and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZF}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZF}\\)</span> (its Zermelo--Fraenkel theory code)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I^{M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\">\\(I^{M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\\)</span> (the canonical carrier and relation-interpretation projections, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-structure.md\">../batch18/58-df-structure.md</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}_S\\)</span> (model predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"923884eb8fe4e61d\" href=\"?note=923884eb8fe4e61d\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-model.md\">../batch09/58-df-model.md</a>)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L_{\\in}\\coloneqq\\mathcal L_{\\in}\">\\(L_{\\in}\\coloneqq\\mathcal L_{\\in}\\)</span>，固定成员语言取 <code>58-df-first-order-language</code>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZF}\">\\(\\mathrm{ZF}\\)</span> 取 <code>58-ax-zfc</code>。关系解释中的二元组采用域为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2\">\\(2\\)</span> 的函数编码；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E_M,E_N\">\\(E_M,E_N\\)</span> 是下式转换得到的有序对关系。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}top\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S(M,N)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Model}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\dot\\in\\,\\in L_{\\in}.\\mathrm{Rel}_2\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists A,B,E_M,E_N\\in V\\;\\Biggl[\nA=\\mathrm{Univ}(M)\\land B=\\mathrm{Univ}(N)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land E_M=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in A\\times A:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^M_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_N=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in B\\times B:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^N_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_M\\subseteq A\\times A\\land E_N\\subseteq B\\times B\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land A\\subseteq B\n\\land E_M=E_N\\cap(A\\times A)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\langle b,a\\rangle\\in E_N\\to b\\in A)\n\\Biggr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}top\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S(M,N)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{Model}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\dot\\in\\,\\in L_{\\in}.\\mathrm{Rel}_2\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\exists A,B,E_M,E_N\\in V\\;\\Biggl[\nA=\\mathrm{Univ}(M)\\land B=\\mathrm{Univ}(N)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land E_M=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in A\\times A:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^M_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_N=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in B\\times B:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^N_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_M\\subseteq A\\times A\\land E_N\\subseteq B\\times B\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land A\\subseteq B\n\\land E_M=E_N\\cap(A\\times A)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\langle b,a\\rangle\\in E_N\\to b\\in A)\n\\Biggr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The last clause is the end-extension condition: no new element of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"N\">\\(N\\)</span> lies below an old set of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The former tuple display did not connect its advertised carrier and membership relation to the canonical projections used by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}_S\\)</span>. The repaired definition reads those components from the actual structure codes, so model satisfaction and the top-extension relation refer to the same interpretations.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md","status":"resolved","id":"a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-ax-zfc.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-model.md","status":"resolved","id":"923884eb8fe4e61d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-model.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-structure.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9b8711cda3f31ca","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-structure.md","status":"resolved","id":"d9b8711cda3f31ca","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Univ}$ and $I^{M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}$ (the canonical carrier and relation-interpretation projections, see [[../batch18/58-df-structure.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-model.md","status":"resolved","id":"923884eb8fe4e61d","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Model}_S$ (model predicate, see [[../batch09/58-df-model.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"M,N\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"L_{\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"\\dot\\in","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZF}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Univ}","display":false},{"tex":"I^{M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Model}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"L_{\\in}\\coloneqq\\mathcal L_{\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZF}","display":false},{"tex":"2","display":false},{"tex":"E_M,E_N","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}model\\text{-}top\\text{-}extension}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{ZfcModelTopExtension}_S(M,N)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathrm{Model}_S(M,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}_S(N,\\mathrm{ZF},L_{\\in})\n\\land\\dot\\in\\,\\in L_{\\in}.\\mathrm{Rel}_2\\\\\n&\\land\\exists A,B,E_M,E_N\\in V\\;\\Biggl[\nA=\\mathrm{Univ}(M)\\land B=\\mathrm{Univ}(N)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land E_M=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in A\\times A:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^M_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_N=\\{\\langle a,b\\rangle\\in B\\times B:\\{\\langle0,a\\rangle,\\langle1,b\\rangle\\}\\in I^N_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\\}\n\\land E_M\\subseteq A\\times A\\land E_N\\subseteq B\\times B\\\\\n&\\quad\\land A\\subseteq B\n\\land E_M=E_N\\cap(A\\times A)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\forall a\\in A\\;\\forall b\\in B\\;\n(\\langle b,a\\rangle\\in E_N\\to b\\in A)\n\\Biggr].\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"N","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Model}_S","display":false}],"bytes":2407,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-2713","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch01/58-df-zfc-model-top-extension.md|58-df-zfc-model-top-extension]]（batch01）"}],"outgoing":["a3348ed9eb6fb4e3","923884eb8fe4e61d","d9b8711cda3f31ca"]}